.claude/specs/02-SGS-BLOCKS-REFERENCE.md
# The knowledge-base DB always lives OUTSIDE this repo (~/.agents/skills/sgs-wp-engine/,
# symlinked from ~/.claude/skills/). Any sgs-framework.db appearing INSIDE the repo is a
# stray: sqlite3.connect() silently CREATES an empty file when a path resolves wrongly,
# so an ad-hoc command run from the wrong working directory leaves a 0-byte decoy that a
# later script could open instead of the real database.
#
# This single wildcard replaces two reactive exact-path entries (.claude/ and
# scripts/orchestrator/) that were each patched in after a previous leak — and which
# still missed the two found on 2026-08-02 (scripts/ and the skills scripts/ dir).
# Four leak sites, four different working directories: whack-a-mole was losing.
**/sgs-framework.db

# Spec 33 extractor runtime artifacts (live-payload backups + pre-deploy working copies)
sites/*/theme-snapshot-backups/
sites/*/theme-snapshot.pre-*.json

# Claude Design mega-menu draft ZIPs — extracted folders are committed; the zips stay local (Bean 2026-07-24)
sites/*.zip

# Scratch / tool artefacts (2026-08-08 cleanup)
.superpowers/
plugins/sgs-blocks/scripts/.coverage
plugins/sgs-blocks/scripts/parity/__fluid_selftest_fixtures__/

# Third-party reference checkouts and scratch output that live inside the plugin
# dir but are NOT part of it. Untracked files are INVISIBLE to build-deploy.py's
# dirty gate (it reads `git status` tracked files) yet VISIBLE to tar, so without
# this they ship to the canary. Proven 2026-08-27 with a controlled tar test:
# `--exclude=plugins/sgs-blocks/src` is path-anchored and does NOT match
# `plugins/sgs-blocks/stackable/src`, so 278MB of a competitor's GPL tree would
# have been uploaded into the live plugin directory, web-accessible.
plugins/sgs-blocks/stackable/
plugins/sgs-blocks/now.tmp.json
